WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.890
You do not need a paid stack to start.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.459
Free tools are enough for your first offers.

00:00:05.459 --> 00:00:08.029
This lesson is about tools you actually need.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:08.992
Free stack first.

00:00:08.992 --> 00:00:11.240
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.451
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.451 --> 00:00:19.269
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:22.801
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:26.976
Stay practical: pick a minimum tool stack before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.296 --> 00:00:36.718
Minimum stack: notes app, calendar, email or messaging, a simple page or doc for your offer, and a way to take payment when someone says yes.

00:00:36.718 --> 00:00:39.618
Remember the objective: pick a minimum tool stack.

00:00:39.618 --> 00:00:43.604
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:43.604 --> 00:00:47.953
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:47.953 --> 00:00:51.939
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:51.939 --> 00:00:56.288
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:56.608 --> 00:01:01.937
Skip fancy CRM, brand kits, and automation until a real customer forces the need.

00:01:01.937 --> 00:01:04.982
Remember the objective: pick a minimum tool stack.

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:09.170
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.738
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:17.925
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:22.493
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:22.493 --> 00:01:25.157
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:26.680
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.761
Pick one tool per job.

00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:31.227
If you already have it, keep it.

00:01:31.227 --> 00:01:32.988
Switching tools is not progress.

00:01:32.988 --> 00:01:35.806
Remember the objective: pick a minimum tool stack.

00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:39.680
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.907
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:43.907 --> 00:01:47.781
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:47.781 --> 00:01:52.008
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:52.328 --> 00:01:55.777
In the quiz, you will pick a minimum tool stack.

00:01:55.777 --> 00:02:00.606
In the quiz, you will practice until you can pick a minimum tool stack.

00:02:00.606 --> 00:02:01.296
Answer carefully.

00:02:01.296 --> 00:02:04.400
If you miss one, review the idea and retry.

